6`.\n- Expected values in `tests/test_money.py` match half-even: 2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66.\n\nReviewer: alex", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 371393, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Sx3RoMLqAWa86QawC3RdUz", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 371393, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Sx3RoMLqAWa86QawC3RdUz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373157, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Root cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 and the function's docstring call for banker's rounding.\n- **Change:** on branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That is a one-line change plus the matching import.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner under org policy, so that step is still open.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the two files involved and checking the repo layout.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RPntsKxrddFRC6MButm1La", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01S4Fk42DJxsMDuFPyEqLcVV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TyG8f1Xt1y84uPFFfwao8k", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. The test expectations agree with half-even (2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66). I'll create the branch and make that one-line change.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CCsVqwYTA6iN5fQE8yxkRu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014suJGXTDBwwT5q9pj881dc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money was using ROUND_HALF_UP, contrary to the banker's rounding\nrequirement in FIN-212 and the function docstring. Switch to ROUND_HALF_EVEN\nso tests/test_money.py passes.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is committed. Next I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01E8UZQqnHhabBF1wgmzBCC7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "c